      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. Regarding the 'unusual textural changes' I mentioned—we have some cases where the skin feels almost leathery or has these small, bumpy protrusions that seem to appear randomly across the surface. It's a very peculiar, almost 'gnarly' look. Is there a specific set of ICD-10 subcategories for these types of irregular, bumpy surfaces, or do we typically group those under more general descriptors like 'lichenoid' or 'verrucous'?",
