      "content": "ICD-10 does not contain a single comprehensive subcategory for \"leathery\" or \"bumpy\" textures, so these features must be mapped to existing descriptive terms like 'lichenoid' (L74-L81), 'verrucous' (L61-L62), or 'xerotic' (L80) depending on the specific clinical context. You should select the code that best matches the predominant structure among these established categories while always cross-referencing the documentation to ensure the specific texture described was clinically confirmed. If the textural changes do not align with standard descriptors or represent a unique syndrome, a catch-all code for unspecified exophytic growth or a general code for unspecified skin disorder may be necessary.",
